      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zionhill%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community lies on Old Bethlehem Pike, just east of the Unami Creek, a small local waterway that winds through the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zionhill%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Because Zionhill is unincorporated, it does not have its own city or town government; instead, it relies on Springfield Township for services.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://kids.kiddle.co/Zionhill,_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Zionhill is described as a cluster of homes and businesses that blend into the surrounding countryside of southeastern Pennsylvania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
